 Smita (Minutes 7:00 – 10:00)
I am Smita, and I am presenting the CI/CD pipeline, model registry, and inference workflows.
The CI/CD pipeline automates testing, training, evaluation, registration, and deployment.
CodeBuild performs dependency installation and unit testing.
The SageMaker Pipeline is triggered after successful build validation.
The pipeline executes five defined steps in a DAG structure.
In a successful pipeline execution, preprocessing, parallel training, evaluation, and conditional checks all succeed.
The ConditionStep evaluates whether model accuracy meets or exceeds 0.75.
If the condition evaluates to TRUE, the model is registered in the Model Registry.
The model package is then automatically approved and deployed to an endpoint.
In a failed execution scenario, if a training step fails, downstream steps do not start.
The DAG clearly displays the failure state and provides debugging information.
The SageMaker Model Registry ensures version control and governance.
Each registered model is versioned and tracked.
Approval status transitions from PendingManualApproval to Approved before deployment.
Real-time inference is performed using a SageMaker endpoint deployed on ml.m5.large instance type.
The endpoint accepts 13 comma-separated feature values in text/csv format.
The output is a probability score between 0 and 1.
A threshold of 0.5 determines the final binary classification.
Batch inference is implemented using SageMaker Batch Transform.
The input file must exclude the label column and contain only feature values.
The output predictions are stored in the batch-output S3 prefix.
This validates large-scale inference capability.
Future improvements include implementing patient-level data splitting to prevent potential leakage.
AUC equal to 1.0 indicates possible data leakage risk and requires further investigation.
Scalability improvements include enabling auto-scaling policies and multi-region deployment.
Bias mitigation requires subgroup analysis by gender and age_group.
Ethical risk mitigation includes adjusting thresholds to reduce false negatives.
This system must always be used under clinical supervision and not as an autonomous diagnostic tool.
This concludes the complete end-to-end demonstration of our liver disease classification ML system built on Amazon SageMaker.
Thank you.
